mcqs.append(q("mcq-crim-01-004", "ch-crim-01", "top-crim-01-01", "Under Section 1(5) BNS / Section 4 IPC, extraterritorial jurisdiction extends to offences committed by:", ["Only Indian citizens within India", "Any citizen of India in any place without and beyond India", "Foreign nationals in foreign countries against foreigners", "Diplomatic officers with immunity"], 1, "B", "Section 1(5) applies to any citizen of India in any place without and beyond India.", {"A": "Too narrow.", "B": "Correct; Indian citizens committing crimes anywhere are triable in India.", "C": "Requires jurisdictional nexus.", "D": "Diplomats enjoy immunity."}, "Medium", "BNS Section 1(5)", "Master extraterritorial jurisdiction."))
mcqs.append(q("mcq-crim-01-005", "ch-crim-01", "top-crim-01-01", "A, a foreigner, commits murder on an Indian merchant ship on the high seas. Which court in India has jurisdiction to try A?", ["No Indian court has jurisdiction", "Any court in India where A may be found or brought", "Only the Supreme Court of India", "Only the International Court of Justice"], 1, "B", "Under Section 1(5)(b) BNS / S. 4(2) IPC, jurisdiction covers any person on an Indian registered ship.", {"A": "Indian courts have jurisdiction by registration.", "B": "Correct; triable where found in India.", "C": "SC is not original trial court.", "D": "ICJ is for states, not criminal trials."}, "Medium", "BNS Section 1(5)(b)", "Analyze maritime jurisdiction over foreign nationals."))
mcqs.append(q("mcq-crim-01-006", "ch-crim-01", "top-crim-01-01", "Which of the following acts cannot be punished under the general provisions of BNS 2023?", ["Offences in India by foreign citizens", "Offences in Jammu and Kashmir", "Mutiny and desertion governed by Army Act, 1950", "Economic offences in territorial waters"], 2, "C", "Section 1(6) BNS / Section 5 IPC preserves special military enactments.", {"A": "Foreign citizens subject to territorial law.", "B": "J&K covered by BNS.", "C": "Correct; Army Act is preserved.", "D": "Territorial waters are part of India."}, "Medium", "BNS Section 1(6)", "Understand savings of special penal laws."))
mcqs.append(q("mcq-crim-01-007", "ch-crim-01", "top-crim-01-01", "In Mobarik Ali Ahmed v. State of Bombay (1957), the Supreme Court affirmed that a foreigner committing an offence in India while physically outside India is:", ["Immune from trial", "Amenable to Indian criminal jurisdiction as the offence occurred in India", "Liable only to civil damages", "Subject only to extradition without trial"], 1, "B", "Physical presence in India is not necessary if the crime took effect in India.", {"A": "No immunity.", "B": "Correct; corporeal presence not required.", "C": "Penal liability applies.", "D": "Trial is competent in India."}, "Hard", "AIR 1957 SC 857", "Apply extraterritorial precedent."))
